---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { REPO } from "../../consts";
---

<Base title="Quickstart" description="Parse your first input with tabnas in five minutes.">
  <article class="qs">
    <p class="eyebrow">Quickstart</p>
    <h1>Your first parse, in five minutes</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Install the engine, define a three-line grammar in ABNF, and parse a
      string into a value. TypeScript here; the Go path mirrors it exactly.
    </p>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h2>1 · Install</h2>
        <pre><code>npm install @tabnas/parser @tabnas/abnf</code></pre>
      </li>

      <li>
        <h2>2 · Define a grammar</h2>
        <p>An addition grammar, written in ABNF — <code>NR</code> is the built-in
          number token, <code>[ … ]</code> is optional, and the rule refers to
          itself to handle a whole chain.</p>
        <pre><code>{`import { Tabnas } from '@tabnas/parser'
import { abnf } from '@tabnas/abnf'

const tn = new Tabnas({ plugins: [abnf] })
tn.abnf(\`
  add = NR [ PL add ]
  PL  = "+"
\`, {
  actions: {
    '@add:o:NR': (r) => {
      // accumulate the running total onto the outermost \\'add\\'
      let top = r; while (top.parent && top.parent.name === 'add') top = top.parent
      top.node.value = (top.node.value || 0) + Number(r.o[0].val)
    },
  },
})`}</code></pre>
      </li>

      <li>
        <h2>3 · Parse</h2>
        <pre><code>{`tn.parse('1+2+3').value   // => 6
tn.parse('12+3+45').value // => 60`}</code></pre>
      </li>

      <li>
        <h2>4 · Verify</h2>
        <p>See the raw tree — every parse has the same
          <code>{"{ rule, src, kids }"}</code> shape:</p>
        <pre><code>{`tn.parse('1+2')
// => { rule: 'add', src: '1+2', kids: [ { rule: 'PL', src: '+', kids: [] }, … ] }`}</code></pre>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="next">
      <h2>Next steps</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/playground">Open the playground</a> and edit this grammar live.</li>
        <li><a href="/docs">Browse the docs</a> — tutorials, reference, and concepts for every package.</li>
        <li>Read the tested examples in the
          <a href={`${REPO("abnf")}#readme`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">@tabnas/abnf</a> and
          <a href={`${REPO("parser")}#readme`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">@tabnas/parser</a> READMEs.</li>
        <li>Building in Go? The same grammar and tree are available via
          <code>github.com/tabnas/parser/go</code>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .qs { max-width: 44rem; }
  .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.16em; color: var(--accent); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .qs h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); text-wrap: balance; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .lede { font-size: 1.2rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 2rem 0; display: grid; gap: 1.75rem; }
  .steps h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .steps p { color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .next { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .next li { margin: 0.4rem 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
